    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d236">

                <pb facs="0261" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862K.6377/7–347: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Political Adviser in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Atcheson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-07-03T21:00:00-04:00">July 3, 1947—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>255. Reurtel 175 June 29.<anchor n="15" xml:id="d236-f1"/> Reference Angaur
                    project SecState at July 2 press conference made fol statement:</p>
                <p>[Here follows quotation of text printed in Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 13, 1947, page 101.]</p>
                <pb facs="0262" n="248" xml:id="pg248"/>
                <p>Reference Antarctic whaling expedition Dept has consistently supported SCAP’s position in conversations with Ambassadors
                    and other officials interested govts and in press conferences.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
